# Hisaab Banking Chatbot — Cursor Rules

## Project Overview
Hisaab is a Pakistani banking chatbot demo. Node.js/Express backend + React/Vite frontend.
AI is powered by OpenRouter (OpenAI-compatible API) using `google/gemini-2.0-flash-001`.
Persistence is a single JSON file (`backend/data/db.json`) — no real database.

---

## Monorepo Layout

```
v2/
├── backend/          # Node.js + Express (ESM, "type": "module")
│   ├── src/
│   │   ├── server.js            # Entry point — boots Express, registers routes
│   │   ├── config/config.js     # All env vars in one place
│   │   ├── auth/
│   │   │   ├── authService.js   # bcrypt login, credential check
│   │   │   └── sessions.js      # In-memory session Map, conversationHistory per session
│   │   ├── chatbot/
│   │   │   ├── geminiAgent.js   # AI agent: OpenRouter tool-calling loop, option inference
│   │   │   ├── toolDefinitions.js  # OpenAI-format tool schemas (9 tools)
│   │   │   ├── toolExecutor.js  # Routes tool names → backend operations, builds receipts
│   │   │   ├── intentEngine.js  # Regex-based NLP: intent detection + entity extraction
│   │   │   ├── flowUtils.js     # Text-matching helpers (accounts, beneficiaries, bills)
│   │   │   └── flows/           # Legacy FSM flows (superseded by AI agent, kept for ref)
│   │   ├── data/
│   │   │   ├── repository.js    # All DB read/write ops; atomic JSON writes via writeChain
│   │   │   └── seed.js          # Initial demo data (users, accounts, beneficiaries, bills, cards)
│   │   ├── middleware/
│   │   │   ├── requireSession.js  # Bearer token → session lookup; attaches req.session
│   │   │   └── errorHandler.js    # Global error handler + 404
│   │   ├── routes/
│   │   │   ├── auth.js          # POST /api/auth/login, POST /api/auth/logout, GET /api/auth/me
│   │   │   └── chat.js          # GET /api/chat/bootstrap, POST /api/chat
│   │   ├── services/
│   │   │   └── transactionService.js  # debitAccount() — updates balance + appends transaction
│   │   └── utils/
│   │       ├── errors.js        # AppError, SessionExpiredError
│   │       ├── logger.js        # Structured console logger (INFO/WARN/ERROR)
│   │       └── refId.js         # generateRefId(), formatPKR()
│   ├── .env                     # Secrets (never commit)
│   └── data/db.json             # Live JSON database (auto-seeded on first run)
│
└── frontend/         # React 18 + Vite + Tailwind CSS
    └── src/
        ├── main.jsx             # React entry
        ├── App.jsx              # Auth gate: LoginScreen → ChatScreen
        ├── screens/
        │   ├── LoginScreen.jsx  # userId + password form
        │   └── ChatScreen.jsx   # Main chat UI — messages, options, receipts, composer
        ├── components/
        │   ├── MessageBubble.jsx    # Chat bubble (user/assistant) + TypingIndicator
        │   ├── ButtonOptions.jsx    # Horizontal scrollable option buttons
        │   ├── Composer.jsx         # Always-enabled text input (disabled only while thinking)
        │   ├── ReceiptCard.jsx      # Structured receipt cards for completed operations
        │   ├── Header.jsx           # App header with session countdown
        │   └── SessionExpiredOverlay.jsx
        ├── hooks/useSessionTimer.js # Countdown timer, fires callback on expiry
        ├── services/api.js          # fetch wrapper; token in sessionStorage
        └── utils/format.js
```

---

## API Endpoints

| Method | Path | Auth | Description |
|--------|------|------|-------------|
| POST | `/api/auth/login` | — | `{ userId, password }` → `{ token, user, sessionTimeoutMs }` |
| POST | `/api/auth/logout` | Bearer | Destroys session |
| GET | `/api/auth/me` | Bearer | Returns `{ user }` |
| GET | `/api/chat/bootstrap` | Bearer | Returns greeting + 5-button main menu; resets history |
| POST | `/api/chat` | Bearer | `{ text?, optionValue? }` → `{ response: { messages, options, receipt }, sessionRemainingMs }` |
| GET | `/health` | — | `{ status: "ok", uptime }` |

---

## AI Agent Architecture (`chatbot/geminiAgent.js`)

The agent uses the OpenAI SDK pointed at OpenRouter:
```js
new OpenAI({ baseURL: 'https://openrouter.ai/api/v1', apiKey: config.openrouterApiKey })
```

**Tool-calling loop per turn:**
1. Build messages = `[system, ...truncatedHistory, newUserMessage]`
2. Call `client.chat.completions.create({ model, messages, tools, tool_choice: 'auto' })`
3. If `message.tool_calls` → execute each via `executeTool()`, append `role: 'tool'` results, loop
4. When model returns plain text → extract text, infer UI buttons, extract receipt, return

**Session history format** (stored in `sessions.js`):
- Everything except the system prompt — i.e., `messages.slice(1)` after each turn
- System prompt is prepended fresh each request
- Max 40 entries; always trimmed at a user-text boundary

**Option inference** (`inferOptions(text, toolCallLog)`):
- Confirmation question detected → Yes/No buttons
- `getAccounts` with >1 account + "which account" text → account selection buttons
- `getCards` with active cards + "which card" text → card selection buttons
- Mutating tool succeeded → main menu (5 buttons)
- Otherwise → null

---

## The 9 Tools

| Tool | Mutates | Returns receipt |
|------|---------|-----------------|
| `getAccounts` | No | No |
| `getBalance` | No | No |
| `getBeneficiaries` | No | No |
| `transferFunds` | Yes | `transfer_success` |
| `getBills` | No | No |
| `payBill` | Yes | `bill_success` |
| `getTransactions` | No | `transaction_list` |
| `getCards` | No | No |
| `blockCard` | Yes | `card_blocked` |

Mutating tools (`transferFunds`, `payBill`, `blockCard`) must only be called **after** explicit user confirmation ("yes", "haan", "confirm"). This is enforced in the system prompt and tool descriptions.

---

## Data Model (db.json)

```js
{
  users: [{
    userId, passwordHash, fullName, email,
    accounts: [{ accountId, title, type, maskedNumber, balance, currency }],
    beneficiaries: [{ id, nickname, fullName, bank, maskedNumber }]
  }],
  bills: [{ billerId, userId, billerName, category, accountNumber, currentDue, dueDate }],
  transactions: [{ refId, userId, accountId, type, amount, description, timestamp, balanceAfter, meta }],
  cards: [{ cardId, userId, accountId, type, network, last4, maskedNumber, expiryDate, status, blockedAt? }],
  logs: [{ ts, userId, action, outcome, ...meta }]
}
```

**Demo credentials:**
- `user1` / `password123` — has 2 accounts, 3 beneficiaries, 2 bills, 3 cards
- `user2` / `securepass456` — has 1 account, 1 card

---

## Frontend Chat Flow

```
App.jsx
  └── LoginScreen  →  api.login()  →  tokenStore.set(token)  →  ChatScreen
        └── useEffect: api.bootstrap() → greeting + 5 options
              └── ChatScreen state:
                    messages[]         — all bubbles
                    activeOptions[]    — current button row (null = none)
                    isThinking         — disables Composer + buttons
              └── sendText(text) / sendOption(opt) → api.chat() → applyResponse()
```

**Composer** is always enabled (never gated on "expectsFreeText"). It is disabled only when `isThinking === true`.

**ReceiptCard types:** `transfer_success`, `bill_success`, `card_blocked`, `transaction_list`

